exists_ld_soundness [\\leanok: statement-level]\n    locations: src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:245\n    reason: transitive axiom closure includes sorryAx, but the blueprint entry only carries statement-level \\leanok so this is reported as a warning (no proof-level completeness claim was made).\n    axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n  - MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit [\\leanok: statement-level]\n    locations: src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:1559\n    reason: transitive axiom closure includes sorryAx, but the blueprint entry only carries statement-level \\leanok so this is reported as a warning (no proof-level completeness claim was made).\n    axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n  - MIPStarRE.QPBT.marginalPoly_sub_pointMeas_approx_zero [\\leanok: statement-level]\n    locations: src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:372\n    reason: transitive axiom closure includes sorryAx, but the blueprint entry only carries statement-level \\leanok so this is reported as a warning (no proof-level completeness claim was made).\n    axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n\nNo proof-level \\leanok-tagged declarations depend on sorryAx.\n", "prior_full_review": {"id": 5245488540, "node_id": "PRR_kwDOUJyJf88AAAABOKfNnA", "user": {"login": "Dengnifer", "id": 89234078, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjM0MDc4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89234078?u=7a60297a751d9142f3705fd4d6c15e08cfe00d0f&v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=594 head=88d73454b1b276a5be615d646dbd906640d60603 -->\n# Independent review: PR 594 @ 88d73454b1b276a5be615d646dbd906640d60603\n\n## Summary\n\nReviewed the complete seven-path preservation patch against published main at\n`b6c09eb0cb53d791fd6796245a09054073cf0cc1`, beginning with the source\n`thm:pauli` and the unitary/isometry passage in the paper. The four transfer\ninequalities have the claimed constants 2 and 2, without an answer-count\nfactor; the ancilla results have the stated unit-vector and unitary hypotheses.\nThe original `pauli_soundness` signature and its existing `sorry` are unchanged.\nThe refreshed gap note correctly distinguishes the now-proved global-pair and\nprojective extraction constructions from the still-open concrete transfer,\narbitrary-strategy reduction, source-domain comparison, and final theorem.\n\n## Findings\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (changes, S3/C5) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1137` — The `\\proves{thm:pauli}` proof constructs the ancilla isometries and uses Alice's and Bob's range-projection comparisons at lines 1142-1152 and 1191-1215, but its `\\uses` list has no edge to the newly added `thm:pauli-ancilla-intertwining-support` (line 1102), `thm:pauli-isometry-transfer-alice-support` (line 1045), or `thm:pauli-isometry-transfer-bob-support` (line 1073). Thus the blueprint dependency graph disconnects these formalization-only supports from the source theorem they are meant to support, contrary to `docs/blueprint_style_guide.md` (Recording Formalization-Only Lemmas). Fix: explicitly cite the relevant auxiliary results in the final blueprint proof and add their three labels to that proof's `\\uses` list, without marking the source theorem proved in Lean.\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Statement Integrity\n\n- **Paper `thm:pauli`** (`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1426-1447`): universal `a >= 1`, `0 < b < 1`; every admissible tuple and successful arbitrary strategy. Conclusion: two local isometries, a unit auxiliary state, an unsquared state-norm bound and both Pauli-family comparisons on the ideal state, at the stated `delta_qld` error. **Lean `pauli_soundness`** (`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Soundness.lean:42`): same universal-constant and strategy quantifier order; `epsilon >= 0`, finite-dimensional carrier and fixed field model are boundary encodings; the witness contains the isometries and unit auxiliary state, and the conclusion has the unsquared state norm and two answer-summed squared operator distances. **Verdict:** source-shaped statement with faithful boundary hypotheses, not a proved source theorem; the pre-existing `sorry` at line 53 remains.\n- **Five support nodes** (`blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:998-1126`): not named paper results. The four Lean inequalities (`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Soundness/RangeProjection.lean:51-214`) assume a complete POVM, an orthogonal projection fixing the reference vector or an exact isometry intertwining identity, and for bipartite placement two isometries; they bound the squared operator-family error by twice the unprojected error plus twice the squared state error. The ancilla node (`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Soundness/Ancilla.lean:30-104`) assumes a unit ancilla and, for the composite, `Uᴴ * U = 1`; it proves the exact embedding, matrix, and intertwining identities. **Verdict:** blueprint matches these explicitly conditional *auxiliary* signatures and their proof-level `\\leanok` markers, not `thm:pauli`. None makes a source-level claim or inserts its hypotheses into `pauli_soundness`.\n\n## Verification And Limits\n\n- Independently read the seven-path merge-base diff and entire mathematical additions, dated audit, and relevant telemetry provenance; checked the paper at `08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1426-1447` and `14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1666-1875`, plus trusted-main review and blueprint policies. No PR 595 source or reviewer work was used.\n- `git diff b6c09eb0..HEAD --check` passed; `lake env lean` on RangeProjection, Ancilla, and root Soundness passed (only the known root `sorry` warning). Scoped `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness.Ancilla` compiled both new modules. Direct `#print axioms` for all ten public declarations gave only `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; the author packet's two private-declaration probes report the same closure. The two new modules contain no `sorry`, `admit`, or axiom declaration. The contractions reuse the existing complete-POVM square bound and `DistanceCalculus.sum_norm_mul_apply_le`, while the ancilla proofs use the established vector-tensor and isometry API.\n- Did not rerun full build, CI, blueprint render/sync, rooted axiom audit or the two private axiom probes. Exact-head CI reports all nine statuses green (422 seconds); its rooted audit reports 1669 pass, 0 fail, three existing statement-only warnings and no proof-level `sorryAx`. The dated audit preserves the original PR 536 failures and 6020 + 1903 + 48 second prior cost accounting as historical, not current gate failures.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/594#pullrequestreview-5245488540", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/594", "author_association": "OWNER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/594#pullrequestreview-5245488540"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/594"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-09-18T07:50:43Z", "commit_id": "88d73454b1b276a5b